===persian===

گل در گلخانه فصل را گم می‌کند،
و...
گیاه... در حجمِ شیشه‌ای؛
ناباورانه... زمستان را.
مرا از پنجره‌ات مران...
زمستان سختی پشت شیشه‌هاست.
گیاه در گل‌خانه فصل را از یاد می‌بَرَد...
من در هوایِ تو...
کاش سهراب را می‌دیدم...
بی‌گمان...
اکنون می‌داند...
تا طلوع انگور...
چند ساعت راه است.
۱۳۷۱/۷/۶

===machine===

The flower in the greenhouse loses the season,
and...
the plant... inside a volume of glass;
disbelieving... loses the winter.
Do not drive me from your window...
There is a hard winter behind the panes.
The plant in the greenhouse forgets the season...
and I, in the air of you...
If only I had seen Sohrab...
Beyond doubt...
he knows by now...
how many hours' walking it is
to the rising of the grape.
1371/7/6

===lantern===

The flower in the greenhouse loses the season,
and the plant, inside its volume of glass,
disbelieving, loses the winter.
Do not drive me from your window —
there is a hard winter behind the panes.
The plant in the greenhouse forgets the season;
I, in the air of you...
If only I had seen Sohrab.
Beyond doubt
he knows by now
how many hours' walking it is
to the rising of the grape.

1371/7/6

===translation===

===footnotes===

Sohrab Sepehri — poet and painter, dead in 1980 — is one of the presences this part of the
book keeps circling. He is named outright here, his collection *The Green Volume* gives page 143 its
dateline, and page 161 drinks 'Sohrab's gift, the water in the moon-filled glass.'

The word حجم, *volume*, is Sepehri's: the glass volume the plant sits inside is his title, put in
the poem two lines before his name.
